# Phase 158: Architecture Linter (Import-Graph Rules)

Date: 2026-09-15
Status: DRAFT
Parent DEC: 2026-0915-001 (points #10/#11 — Fitness Rules + Linter)

---

## 1. Problem

Architecture drift queries (/sdd-drift) compare declared vs
observed reality, but nothing enforces structural rules BEFORE
merge: banned imports (domain → infrastructure), layer shortcuts
(API → database), and coupling rules pass silently until a manual
drift round catches them.

## 2. Solution

A spec-level Architecture Linter: declarative fitness rules over
the import/dependency graph, checked in CI as a gate, failing the
pipeline on violation — AI mistakes are caught mechanically, not
by trust.

## 3. Rule Schema

```
RULE AL-<nn>
Scope:   <module/glob path>
MUST NOT import:  <path patterns>
MUST import:      <path patterns>   (optional)
Rationale: @decision.<DEC-id>
Severity: ERROR | WARN
```

Example seed rules (from proposal #10):

```
RULE AL-001
Scope: backend/*/domain
MUST NOT import: backend/*/infrastructure, backend/*/api
Rationale: dependency inversion — domain is innermost
Severity: ERROR

RULE AL-002
Scope: frontend
MUST NOT import: backend/*, */database
Severity: ERROR

RULE AL-003
Scope: */application
MUST import: allowed via domain only; NOT infrastructure directly
Severity: ERROR
```

## 4. Flow

```
AI → code with bad dependency
        ↓
CI: architecture lint (import graph vs rules)
        ↓
FAIL → blocked merge; finding routed to RF (refactor loop)
```

## 5. Rules

- [AL1] Rules live in `.sdd/projects/<name>/architecture/fitness.sdd`
  — human-authored surface ([R109] routing analogy).
- [AL2] Every rule MUST carry a rationale referencing a DEC.
- [AL3] ERROR severity blocks merge (CODE-QUALITY-GATE extension);
  WARN surfaces in /sdd-drift reports.
- [AL4] The linter is adapter code (sdd-adapter) reading the spec;
  spec is source of truth, never the reverse.
- [AL5] Violations found in existing code enter the drift backlog
  (near-duplicate: architecture-drift query), not auto-fix.

## 6. Location

- Spec: `.sdd/projects/<name>/architecture/fitness.sdd` (instance)
- Scaffolding: `templates/_sdd/architecture/fitness.sdd`
- Runtime: `sdd-adapter/architecture-linter.ts` (C1 scope — after
  S1 approval; runs in Docker [R102])

## 7. Integration

- cicd-pipeline.sdd: new gate step ARCH LINT after SEC steps
- /sdd-drift: WARN-severity findings appear in reports
- CODE-QUALITY-GATE: ERROR-severity failures block
